# classic page.pdl: how the 40-tile classic board is DRAWN as an editor page (milestone M11-lite, 2026-11-08). A projection: it decides no rule. Same grammar as the app-level page.pdl (the mini ruleset keeps that one).
# 40 tiles = 4 x (side - 1) with side 11, block 3 -> a 33 x 33 page. Atlas indexes (from looking at the 43-tile atlas): 1 grass 2 planks 3 pond 5 sand 7 sand 12 castle 16 blue-roof house 17 blue tower 19..27 village 28 purple hall
# 29 grey hall 32 dirt 33 sword sign 34 door 35 orange 36 rough stone 37 dark boards 38 blue tile 40 orange diamond 41 white stone. Stand-ins, not art. Every block is one voxel high; buildings are decorations (house and hotel cells).
HEADER  | tile_px     | 24
HEADER  | atlas_cols  | 16
HEADER  | atlas_tiles | 43
HEADER  | rock_slot   | 36
PAGE    | block       | 3
TILEMAP | floor       | 2
TILEMAP | go          | 33
TILEMAP | jail        | 34
TILEMAP | free        | 3
TILEMAP | gotojail    | 13
TILEMAP | chance      | 20
TILEMAP | chest       | 29
TILEMAP | tax         | 37
TILEMAP | group0      | 32
TILEMAP | group1      | 38
