TILEMAP | token_p6   | 23
TILEMAP | token_p7   | 25
TILEMAP | token_p8   | 27
# LABELS (2026-11-09): the names written ON the board. `deskopoly page` bakes each label into the floor texture (3D and 2D from one description, zero per-frame cost). Nothing in C names a tile or a place.
#   LABELS     | on|off              off = the page is byte-identical to the unlabelled one (default on, and only with a real atlas argument)
#   LABELCOLOR | text|outline | rrggbb   glyph colour and the 1 px outline round it (default ffffff / 000000)
#   LABEL      | <tile id or kind> | <text>   display text; a tile's own row beats its kind's row; no row = the tile's own id; empty text = no label; a literal \n forces a line break. Long text wraps (up to 3 lines at
#                                    the biggest font that fits, else smaller fonts, then more lines), so a rename is ONE edit here and no C change. Tile ids (board.pdl: 1 to 16 characters, typed in commands) are NOT touched.
LABELS     | on
LABELCOLOR | text    | ffffff
LABELCOLOR | outline | 000000
# --- PLACEHOLDERS (owner decision 2026-11-09: generic spiral-themed stand-ins until the real Centroid University lore names exist). REMOVAL CONDITION: the owner's lore names replace these rows. NOTHING else may depend on them:
# --- no command, ledger row, test pin or chat parse reads a label; the ids in board.pdl stay (Orange3, Fund2 ...). Colour groups share a word so they stay recognisable.
# Words of 6 letters or fewer get the biggest font (a longer word drops to the next smaller font tier, still readable); that is why these stand-ins use short words.
# The two decks (the owner's own words): Luck and Lost & Found.
LABEL | chance   | Luck
LABEL | chest    | Lost & Found
# corners
LABEL | Start    | Spiral Start
